  "configuration_id": "config_027",
  "reason": "The current best (config_039: scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + multiprofile + transformer + weighted, acc 0.725) shows a strong multimodal result, but we have no evidence yet about whether the RNA encoder choice still matters when image information is present. In RNA-only, scvi_n200 clearly outperforms PCA (0.520 vs 0.485 single-profile; the gap likely persists in multi-profile), yet image-only models are very weak (~0.22). Config_027 (pca_n2000 + imagenet_vit_l + multiprofile + transformer + weighted) is a clean single-variable swap of only the RNA encoder relative to config_039, isolating the contribution of the learned RNA representation in the multimodal setting. If PCA + image approaches scvi + image, the image modality is carrying most of the signal and we can simplify the RNA pipeline; if it falls well short, the scvi representation remains critical even with image fusion. This is the highest-information next step because it directly tests whether the most expensive design choice (RNA encoder) is still necessary, and the result will guide whether subsequent experiments should focus on image-encoder quality, fusion strategy, or other axes."
}

